CAT = "cacoreLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("Under the Wildlife Act, what must a person hold to hunt wildlife in British Columbia?",
 "A hunting licence", ["A firearm storage permit", "A guide's certificate for the area", "A campsite reservation receipt"],
 "Section 11 makes it an offence to hunt without the licences, permits and authorizations the law requires. A hunting licence is the starting point."),
("Which of these is an offence under the Wildlife Act?",
 "Hunting outside the open season", ["Hunting from a ground blind in season", "Hunting on foot with a legal bow", "Waiting beside a game trail at dawn"],
 "The Wildlife Act prohibits hunting at a time not within the open season. Hunting from a blind or on foot, with a lawful weapon, is not covered by that rule."),
("Which of these actions is prohibited by section 27 of the Wildlife Act?",
 "Shooting from a motor vehicle", ["Glassing for game from a parked truck", "Hunting on foot along a quiet road", "Carrying an unloaded rifle in a case"],
 "Section 27 makes it an offence to discharge a firearm, or wound or kill wildlife, from a motor vehicle. Glassing or carrying a cased firearm is not shooting."),
("A hunter fires without regard for others nearby, in open season, on Crown land. The Act treats this as:",
 "Dangerous hunting", ["A matter of etiquette only", "Lawful on public land", "A minor weather risk"],
 "Section 28 makes hunting without reasonable consideration for the lives, safety and property of others an offence. Open season and public land do not excuse it."),
("Where does the Wildlife Act prohibit discharging a firearm?",
 "Across a travelled highway", ["Inside a legal hunting blind", "On the far side of a gravel pit", "In an open season hunting area"],
 "The Act prohibits discharging a firearm on or across the travelled portion of a highway. Check the rules for any road before you shoot near it."),
("What is a designated no shooting area?",
 "Where firearms may not be fired", ["A place where hunting is always free", "A place where only bows are legal", "A place closed to every hiker"],
 "Discharging a firearm in a no shooting area is an offence under the Act. Such areas protect people living or recreating nearby."),
("Who must consent before you hunt over cultivated land?",
 "The owner, lessee or occupier", ["A neighbour on the next farm", "A municipal clerk or the mayor", "Any hiker passing on the road"],
 "Consent must come from the owner, lessee or occupier of the land. The Act does not change the Trespass Act, which can apply to other private land."),
("After shooting an animal, what does the Act require of the hunter?",
 "Reasonable efforts to retrieve it", ["A written report within one week", "Moving the animal off the road", "Leaving the animal for scavengers"],
 "The Act requires every reasonable effort to retrieve killed or wounded wildlife and, for game, to remove the edible portions of the carcass."),
("What does the Act say about edible meat from big game you kill?",
 "Take the edible portions", ["Keep only the head and hide", "Leave all meat in the field", "Donate it all to a charity"],
 "Section 35 requires hunters to remove the edible portions of game. Leaving good meat to spoil is wasteful and illegal."),
("What supervision does a hunter under 18 need in BC?",
 "A qualified adult close by", ["A friend of about the same age", "A parent who waits at home", "Hunting in daylight hours only"],
 "The Act requires close personal supervision by a qualified adult for a hunter under 18. Daylight and a friend of the same age do not satisfy it."),
("Which of these may you do around dangerous wildlife under the Act?",
 "Keep food and garbage secured", ["Leave food out in a campground", "Offer natural foods to bears", "Feed a hungry cougar"],
 "Section 33.1 prohibits intentionally feeding or trying to feed dangerous wildlife. Food rewards make bears and cougars bolder around people."),
("Selling wildlife meat without authorization is called:",
 "Trafficking in wildlife", ["Fair game trading practice", "Routine meat sharing", "Normal field processing"],
 "The Act prohibits trafficking in wildlife meat except as the regulations or a permit allow. Giving meat away is different from selling it."),
("You kill an animal by accident while protecting property. What does the Act require?",
 "A prompt report to an officer", ["Hiding it and leaving the area", "Reporting it after the season", "Keeping it as a trophy"],
 "Section 75 requires a prompt report to an officer when wildlife is killed or wounded by accident or to protect life or property."),
("A conservation officer asks where and when you killed an animal. You must:",
 "State both correctly", ["Refuse to answer", "Give your best guess", "Name the nearest town only"],
 "Section 38 requires you to state the locality and date of the kill correctly when an officer asks. Giving false details is an offence."),
("Which animals are protected from hunting while they are swimming?",
 "Big game", ["Ducks and geese only", "Small game only", "Furbearers only"],
 "Section 30 prohibits hunting, wounding or killing big game that is swimming, with limited exceptions. It protects animals that cannot escape."),
("What does the Act say about hunting with a spotlight?",
 "It is generally prohibited", ["It is allowed after sunset", "It is allowed for bears", "It is allowed on private land"],
 "Section 26 prohibits hunting by use or with the aid of a light or illuminating device. A narrow exception covers wildlife that threatens domestic animals on your property."),
("In a wildlife sanctuary, the Act:",
 "Bars hunting", ["Allows hunting in the fall", "Allows hunting with a bow", "Allows hunting above treeline"],
 "The Act prohibits hunting in a wildlife sanctuary. Sanctuaries exist to protect wildlife from hunting pressure."),
("A species is listed as endangered under the Act. Hunting it is:",
 "Prohibited in every area", ["Allowed with a licensed guide", "Allowed in some regions only", "Allowed with a bow and tag"],
 "Section 26 prohibits hunting an endangered or threatened species. Method and region do not change that."),
("The director may prohibit a person from hunting or carrying a firearm. This can follow:",
 "A conviction or suspension", ["Moving to a different town", "A change of mailing address", "A late income tax return"],
 "Section 24 lets the director prohibit a person from hunting, angling or carrying a firearm for a period within the prescribed limits."),
("An animal killed in open season is in your possession. Which parts must stay on it?",
 "The parts set by regulation", ["A handwritten note on paper", "A bright orange ribbon tied on", "The hunter number tag alone"],
 "Section 36 of the Act requires the parts set by regulation, such as proof of sex or species, to stay attached. The Hunting Regulation lists them."),
("Possessing dead wildlife is lawful only when:",
 "Authorized by licence or permit", ["It was found beside the road", "It is already after the season", "Nobody has seen you take it"],
 "Section 33 makes it an offence to possess dead wildlife or a part of it without authorization. Authorization can come from a licence or a permit."),
("Which statement about a hunter's duty toward other people is correct?",
 "Hunt with consideration", ["Hunt only in the remote areas", "Hunt only with a partner", "Hunt only on the weekdays"],
 "Section 28 requires reasonable consideration for the lives, safety and property of others. This applies everywhere, not only near towns."),
("A hunter takes a legal animal in open season without the required licence and tag. The Act treats this as:",
 "An offence", ["A warning only", "Allowed if the animal is legal", "Allowed in open season"],
 "Hunting without the required licences, permits and authorizations is an offence even in open season for a legal animal."),
("What does a hunter's licence allow?",
 "Hunting within the rules it sets", ["Hunting anywhere in Canada", "Hunting any species all year", "Hunting any land without consent"],
 "A BC licence works within the open seasons, limits, areas and conditions that the Act and regulations set. It does not override landowner consent."),
("A cultivated field has no sign posted. May you hunt over it without asking?",
 "No, consent is still needed", ["Yes, if the field is fenced", "Yes, in a legal open season", "Yes, if you hunt small game"],
 "Section 39 requires consent whether or not a sign is posted. Always ask the owner, lessee or occupier first."),
("You reach the limit for a species and keep hunting it. This is:",
 "Prohibited by regulation", ["Allowed with a hunting partner", "Allowed until it gets dark", "Allowed with a bow only"],
 "The Hunting Regulation makes it an offence to keep hunting a species after reaching its daily or seasonal limit."),
("A species is managed by limited entry hunting. What must you also hold?",
 "A limited entry authorization", ["A second hunting licence number", "A signed letter from a landowner", "A trapline registration card"],
 "The Wildlife Act requires any limited entry hunting authorization the regulations call for, in addition to a hunting licence. These authorizations are issued by draw."),
("A parent lets a child hunt with a firearm without the required supervision. Who commits an offence?",
 "The parent or guardian", ["Nobody if the child is licensed", "Only the child", "Only the supervising adult"],
 "The Act makes it an offence for a parent or guardian to permit a child to possess a firearm without the supervision the law requires."),
]
